<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ruleset name="zaakafhandelapp"
    xmlns="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0 http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset_xml_schema.xsd">
    <description>zaakafhandelapp — Conduction PHPMD ruleset (single source: conduction/hydra-gates).</description>

    <!-- No deviations. The two things this app's old ruleset carried on top of
         the central one were both INERT, and dropping them changes nothing:

         1. Four code-size rules (CyclomaticComplexity, NPathComplexity,
            ExcessiveMethodLength, ExcessiveClassLength) were declared a SECOND
            time with looser thresholds as "legacy debt" for
            ConductionNL/zaakafhandelapp#201. PHPMD's RuleSet::addRule() APPENDS
            - it does not replace by name - so the strict declarations stayed
            active and the loose ones ran alongside them. They could never relax
            anything; the effective floor was always the strict threshold.
            Measured: 47 rules resolved, 0 findings, exit 0 - identical to the
            43 rules resolved here.

         2. StaticAccess carried a NESTED
            <exclude-pattern>*/Dashboard/*</exclude-pattern>. PHPMD reads
            exclude-patterns only as direct children of <ruleset> and silently
            discards nested ones (ConductionNL/.github#155), so it suppressed
            nothing - confirmed by resolving the rule set: that StaticAccess
            instance carried no exceptions and the run's only effective
            ignore-pattern came from phpmd-unusedparams.xml.

         Neither was paid off or re-expressed here: there was no live relaxation
         to preserve. #201 remains open against the underlying code. -->
    <rule ref="vendor/conduction/hydra-gates/quality-config/phpmd.xml"/>
</ruleset>
